  "body": "## Additive PHYS53-NCP execution handoff, parent PR #92\n\n**Scope:** The next genuinely incomplete PHYS53 coding task is compiled Rust1.99 *central Coulomb reference* parity on the authenticated 64-core/125-GiB NCP, plus bounded matched-output benchmark. The remote desktop connector is online but its monthly command quota prevents execution from this conversation; **Rust compile and NCP science are NOT_RUN**, not PASS.\n\n**Files actually authored and verified:** isolated `research/hh_phys53_ncp_handoff_20261016/` adds shell scripts to run source-only Rust on NCP, the local SSH launcher using existing `/home/cosmosapjw/.ssh/ncp_key` without copying/printing key material, a strict Python verifier against original 27 independent mpmath high-precision Coulomb references (3 radii), 768/1152 CF depth comparison, 1-vs-8 thread full CSV bit/byte parity, and 12 matched-output benchmark CSVs for 21..4096 ell at depth2048 and 1/2/4/8 threads. All work isolated from native REI owner; no main merge. No finite-depth CF rigorous truncation claim or high-l f64 imaginary-current admission.\n\n**Actual sandbox execution:** retrieved the original frozen 1386 complex128 NPZ (21,029 bytes) from the independent **restored GDrive PHYS52 capsule**, verified SHA256 `f1bd3074950163960cc2011682d013af60f9b17c471bea72ecbc2ffb19e6855d`. Verified earlier PHYS53 ZIP against independent GDrive re-download, SHA256 `f0b0d2c2247631390716efe790b0638a047c589dd56f320438cb4e172a5f82d6`. Existing PHYS53 tests plus 8 new test cases: **25/25 sandbox pytest PASS** (2.62s), Bash syntax 2/2 PASS. Tests use explicitly *synthetic* output fixtures to exercise error detection, not fabricated NCP receipts. New Rust code was not modified; parent PR #92 Rust remains uncompiled here.\n\n**Authorized execution path:** Check `CODEX_HANDOFF_PROMPT.md` and `README_KO.md`; Codex should checkout this PR branch on the authorized Ubuntu desktop, execute `bash research/hh_phys53_ncp_handoff_20261016/scripts/launch_from_local.sh --preflight-only`, then run the same script without options. NCP worker uses fresh isolated `/root/wu088_hh_phys53_XXXXXXXX`, Rust from `$HOME/.cargo/env`, up to 8 threads, 16-GiB virtual memory, `nice +10`, each calculation timed out at 180s. Do not disturb concurrent NCP REI jobs. Verify actual results and only then commit measured receipts and publish a new additive PR.\n\n**Publication identity:** branch head `53916f7c22be6bc684f7c2cac3a8ce43929938a7`, parent `8fe647d4e836204f783e91024f81a3f2c8f46b60`, tree `dda0f88ff9a029c7e61114239ac9ee910665328c`. All 11 added Git blobs were checked against the sandbox exact Git object SHA1: **11/11 BYTE MATCH**.\n\n**Status guard:** noncentral screened *infinite-angular outgoing* DtN, actual driven `xi=Fy-phi`, `sigma(E)`, Maxwellian `k_HH(T)`, `rei_bianchi HH_R10` remain unresolved/OFF. NIST DLMF 33.8.2 supports the infinite continued fraction's convergence, but does not independently certify its finite truncations; 33.23 warns about high-l cancellation. Work stops at C6/C8 handoff rather than claiming remote success.\n\nBackup of the portable source/NPZ/results capsule and provider verification is recorded separately, including any unavailable Dropbox readback.",
